              Combine placements — like a small left-chest logo with a bold back design — to get the most out of your custom shirt.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Subsection 5: Pricing Factors & Saving Tips -->
          <div class="pc-SeoContent-section">
            <h4 class="pc-SeoContent-subheading">What Affects Your Custom T-Shirt Price (and How to Save)</h4>
            <p>
              Your price depends on quantity, garment style, number of print locations, and decoration method. Here is how to maximize your budget:
            </p>
            <ul class="pc-SeoContent-list">
              <li>
                <strong>Order More:</strong> The price per shirt drops noticeably as your quantity increases — transparent tiered pricing applies automatically.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Use Fewer Colors (for screen printing):</strong> Since screen printing involves separate screens per ink color, keeping your design to 1-2 colors provides significant savings for volume runs.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Choose Digital Printing for Smaller Quantities:</strong> If you're ordering a handful of shirts, Direct-to-Film has zero per-color setup charges, making it the most economical choice.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Stick to One Print Location:</strong> Adding a second placement (like a full back print) adds production cost — a single, well-placed graphic keeps your unit price lowest.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <!-- Subsection 6: Groups & Occasions -->
          <div class="pc-SeoContent-section">
            <h4 class="pc-SeoContent-subheading">Custom T-Shirts for Every Group</h4>
            <p>
              Whatever brings your people together, there's a custom t-shirt built for the occasion:
            </p>
